Use cFTModalPanel.pkg         // FT: the dark modal, same base as MaintainLibrariesFT.dg
Use RefactorConstants.h.pkg
Use FTAllWebControlClasses.pkg   // FT: cFTWebForm (editable), cFTWebButton, cFTWebHtmlBox
Use cFTLocalWebControlHost.pkg
Use cFTGridHost.pkg              // FT: the button band - a host on a grid of 8 px columns (RDCFlexTron)
Use File_dlg.pkg
Use FTPageIsUp.pkg               // FTHostPageIsUp - can the field's page take a live push now? (RDCFlexTron)
Use FTMarkupBuilders.pkg         // the HTML vocabulary - OpenHtml, IconLabel, the builders
/*  ADD A PACKAGE - one field that takes all three kinds, as DataFlex Studio 26 does it.

    WHY ONE FIELD (Nils 2026-08-14, describing the Studio's dialog). df-cli's own grammar is a union:
    "package install ... can be repository/package, a git url, or a file path". One box that accepts
    any of the three matches the tool underneath, and it is the only shape that lets a user paste
    something they were given without first deciding which KIND of thing it is.

        Local   <path to an .sws>                     absolute or relative; the Browse button fills it
        Cloud   <publisher>/<package>#<version>       the version is optional, and may be a range
        Git     <gitUrl>/<pathToSws>#<tagOrBranch>    both the path and the ref are optional

    ".git/" is what separates the repository from the path inside it, and "#" always introduces the
    version or ref. Nils's own entries were added this way, e.g.

        https://github.com/NilsSve/Library-DFAbout.git/RDC-DFAbout-Library.sws

    WE DO NOT CLONE ANYTHING, and nothing here downloads. df-cli takes the string, fetches into the
    global package cache (df-cli cache: one shared store per machine, keyed Publisher_Package-Version)
    and writes the dependency into the workspace itself - for a git source, as
    {source, sws, version} with the commit it resolved to. This dialog's whole job is to collect the
    string and hand it over, which keeps the standing rule intact: DFRefactor fetches nothing.

    NO SEARCH HERE. The Studio's dialog says "to browse the available packages close this dialog",
    and the same split applies: this is the ENTRY point, while Browse Packages... on the Libraries
    dialog is the list. A user who knows what they want should not have to browse for it first.  */

/*  The two examples on the Add package dialog - the libraries nearly every legacy workspace carries
    (Nils 2026-08-17). Verified with df-cli package install - vwin32fh again on 2026-08-20, after it
    moved to the NilsSve fork: DataFlexCode's repo has no DF26 header at all (DF190/191/200/201/250
    only), so the DF26.0 name exists solely in the fork. VDFQuery20 moved to the NilsSve build on
    2026-09-05: DataFlexCode's repo bundles a 2003-era vWin32fh.pkg that WINS the search path over
    the vwin32fh package in every workspace carrying both (LegacyApp and WinServ: every Use vWin32fh.pkg,
    the application's own included, resolved to it), while the NilsSve build ships no copy and
    declares the vwin32fh package as its dependency - one string brings both (verified with df-cli
    package install on a fresh workspace the same day). If either upstream renames
    its .sws, the string is refused with "Failed to configure" and this is the one place to correct it.
    Plain, SELECTABLE text to copy into the field - not links (Nils: "should not be links, but it should
    be possible to copy the strings"; the click-to-fill first cut did not fire anyway). */
Define CS_ApExampleVwin32fh for "https://github.com/NilsSve/Library-vwin32fh.git/StudioLibrary/vWin32fh-Library-DF26.0.sws"
Define CS_ApExampleVdfQuery for "https://github.com/NilsSve/VDFQuery20.git/VDFQuery20.sws"
Define CS_ApExampleStables  for "https://github.com/DataFlexCode/Stables20.git/Stables26.sws"
Define CS_ApExampleSigCj    for "https://github.com/NilsSve/Library-SigCj.git/SigCj-Library-DF26.0.sws"

/*  The RDC library shelf (Nils 2026-08-30: "it might encourage users to try out my libraries").

    A DIFFERENT KIND OF ROW from the two above, which is why a rule separates them. Those two are
    what a legacy workspace almost certainly already needs; these are offered, and a row that
    offers has to say what the thing IS - a bare URL persuades nobody. Each carries its own
    one-line description, taken from the repository's own About text rather than invented here.

    THE .sws NAMES ARE VERIFIED, not guessed, because a wrong one is refused with "Failed to
    configure" and this is the one place to correct it. DUF and DataFolderSelector come from a real
    workspace's own dependency list; HolidaysFuncLib was read off the repository (it ships
    24.0/25.0 files beside the package file, which is the one to name). Since 2026-09-25 no RDC
    package name carries a DataFlex version.

    Order is Nils's: DUF first, as the largest and the one that brings three more packages with it. */
Define CS_ApExampleDuf      for "https://github.com/NilsSve/Library-DUF.git/RDC-DUF-Library.sws"
Define CS_ApExampleDfs      for "https://github.com/NilsSve/Library-DataFolderSelector.git/RDC-DataFolderSelector-Library.sws"
Define CS_ApExampleHolidays for "https://github.com/NilsSve/Library-HolidaysFuncLib.git/RDC-Holidays-Functions-Library.sws"
/*  RDCFlexTron joined the shelf 2026-09-25 (Nils: "Add the RDC-FLEXTRON-LIBRARY"), last in line. Its note is
    the package's own description, shortened, plus the one thing its README insists on: a Web UI theme
    package - without one, a FlexTron page waits seconds for a stylesheet that never arrives. The string is
    the source and .sws DFRefactor's own workspace pins. Library-RDCFlexTron is a PRIVATE repository today,
    so the link installs only for an account that can read it. */
Define CS_ApExampleFlexTron for "https://github.com/NilsSve/Library-RDCFlexTron.git/RDC-FlexTron-Library.sws"

/* THE BUTTON BAND IS PINNED, NOT STACKED (Nils 2026-08-15: "the solution implemented was wrong
   ... a new section was added to the bottom ... the buttons are now instead overdrawn by that
   new bottom area").

   The first attempt put OK/Cancel as the LAST ROW of the main host's grid and then made the
   whole dialog taller. That fixes nothing twice over: the help content still pushes the last
   row past the host's bottom edge, and the host's design-time bottom margin becomes a dead
   strip that grows with the dialog - the "new section". Rows stack; they do not pin.

   Now the band is its own host, anchored anBottomLeftRight, so it sits at the dialog's bottom
   edge at every size - and the main host fills exactly the space above it, so there is no dead
   strip for anything to be overdrawn by. However long the help grows, it can only run out of
   room INSIDE the main host; the buttons cannot be pushed anywhere. */

/* TALLER FOR THE LIBRARY SHELF (Nils 2026-08-30: "no vertical scroll-bar so it is easy to miss
   that there are more libraries"). The three added rows and their descriptions ran past the
   content host's bottom edge and were simply clipped - nothing said there was more, which is
   the worst way to lose content. 268 -> 338 fits the whole help block again, 338 -> 358
   made room for a fourth row, RDCFlexTron (2026-09-25), and 358 -> 393 shows all of it again
   (Nils 2026-10-17). Since then the example links scroll in a box of their own (see the help
   box), so a row added later scrolls instead of being cut off. The minimum, 250 x 500, lets
   the dialog be dragged smaller: RDCToolsLib keeps it since 1.0.12 (until then the class set
   the minimum to the design size, over the object's own).

   The three numbers move TOGETHER: the panel's height, the content host's height, and the
   button band's Location. The band touches the content host's bottom on purpose (see its own
   comment - the white resize stripe), so changing one without the others reopens that gap. */
Object oAddPackage_dg is a cFTModalPanel
    Set Label to "Add package"
    Set Location to 2 6
    Set Size to 393 560
    Set piMinSize to 250 500
    Set Icon to "DFRefactor.ico"

    // The workspace being added to - shown, because a package goes into ONE workspace and the user
    // may have arrived here from a copy rather than from the loaded one.
    Property String  psSwsFile ""
    // What the user typed. "" when they cancelled, which is how the caller knows.
    Property String  psPackage ""
    Property Boolean pbConfirmed False
    // Whether OK is currently drawn LIVE. Cached so a keystroke only re-renders the band when the
    // blank/non-blank state actually flips - not on every character.
    Property Boolean pbOkLit False

    /* STATE IS DECLARED ABOVE oWebHost DELIBERATELY. A Property inside an OBJECT comes into existence only
       at the point its declaration is reached during creation, and the controls inside oWebHost run
       "Set psHtml to (...Html(Self))" WHILE being created. A property declared further down the
       object does not exist yet, and the program dies at STARTUP with error 98 "Invalid message" -
       which it did, GET_PSAPCOPIED <- GET_HELPHTML <- SET_PSHTML, when two of them sat beside the
       timer that used them (Nils 2026-08-21). It compiles perfectly either way, because Get ... of
       <handle> resolves at runtime. Keep new state up here. */

    Object oOpenSwsDialog is a OpenDialog
        Set Dialog_Caption to "Select the package workspace file (.sws)"
        Set Filter_String to "DataFlex workspace|*.sws|Any file|*.*"
        Set MultiSelect_State to False
    End_Object

    Object oWebHost is a cFTLocalWebControlHost
        Set Location to 4 4
        Set Size to 351 552
        Set peAnchors to anAll
        Set piColumnCount to 14

        /* THE ONE FIELD. Editable, and every keystroke syncs to psPackage on the PANEL - the OK
           handler lives on a different host, and a cross-host WebGet of a live control value is the
           err-98 path (see CmdLineIniFileExporterFT, which learned this the same way). */
        Object oApPkg_wf is a cFTWebForm
            Set piColumnSpan  to 12
            Set psLabel to "Package:"
            // LEFT, tight (Nils 2026-08-15: "aligning it with the text in the dialog") - the FT
            // default is alignRight in a wide label column, which parked "Package:" mid-air.
            Set peLabelAlign to alignLeft
            Set piLabelOffset to 60
            Set psToolTip to "A publisher/package#version, a git url, or a path to a local .sws. See the notes below."
            Procedure OnChange String sNewValue String sOldValue
                Forward Send OnChange sNewValue sOldValue
                Set psPackage of (oAddPackage_dg(Self)) to sNewValue
                // OK lights the moment there is something to add, dims when there is not.
                Send RefreshOkState of (oAddPackage_dg(Self))
            End_Procedure
        End_Object

        /* The Studio puts a looking-glass at the right end of the field; this is that button.
           A CHIP, not a cFTWebButton (Nils 2026-08-15: "change the font for the Browse button to
           be the same as on the Cancel button ... right aligned with the Cancel button"). The
           framework button wears the theme face; a chip wears .apb - the SAME class Cancel wears,
           so the two cannot drift apart in font or in right edge (both hosts are the same width,
           both rows flex-end with the same padding).

           The price of a chip is the defer: a cWebHtmlBox click runs on the WebView2 pump, and a
           modal file dialog must not open there - so the dialog opens from OnHtmlClick, after the
           click has returned (the library's click relay). */
        Function BrowseChipHtml Returns String
            String sHtml
            Move (CS_PaletteCssLink + CssLink("addpackage")) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (DivOpen("apf")) ;
                + (ClickableHtml("div", "apb", "apbrowse", "", ;
                                 (IconLabel(CS_GlyphScan, "Browse...")), ;
                                 "Browse for a library on disk - its .sws file.")) ;
                + CS_DivEnd) to sHtml
            Function_Return sHtml
        End_Function

        Object oApBrowse_hb is a cFTWebHtmlBox
            Set piColumnIndex to 12
            Set piColumnSpan  to 2
            // DESIGN-TIME PLACEHOLDER for the Studio's Windows Designer, which models the LAST literal
            // psHtml it can parse. It is the string the runtime seeds (dumped by the cFTWebHtmlBox design
            // dump, no workspace loaded); the runtime expression sits in End_Construct_Object below.
            Set psHtml to """
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="RDCFlexTron/palette.css">
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="RDCFlexTron/buttons.css">
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="RDCFlexTron/bars.css">
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="CssStyle/addpackage.css">
            <div class="apf">
                <div class="apb" data-ServerOnClick="apbrowse" title="Browse for a library on disk - its .sws file.">
                    <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                        <path d="M4 7v-1a2 2 0 0 1 2 -2h2 M4 17v1a2 2 0 0 1 2 2h2 M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1 M16 20h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 -2v-1 M5 12l14 0"/></svg>Browse...</div></div>
            """

            // RUNTIME content - here rather than in the object body, so the Designer keeps the literal above.
            Procedure End_Construct_Object
                Forward Send End_Construct_Object
                Set psHtml to (BrowseChipHtml(Self))
            End_Procedure
            // After the web click has returned (the library's click relay): the file dialog opens here.
            Procedure OnHtmlClick String sId String sParam
                If (sId = "apbrowse") ;
                    Send DoBrowseLocal of (oAddPackage_dg(Self))
            End_Procedure
        End_Object

        /* The three formats, spelled out. Long for a dialog, and deliberately so: this is the one
           screen where a user has to know that a git url carries the path to the .sws INSIDE it, and
           being told here is cheaper than a failed install and a trip to the documentation. */
        Function HelpHtml Returns String
            String sHtml sSws

            Get psSwsFile of (oAddPackage_dg(Self)) to sSws

            Move (CS_PaletteCssLink + CssLink("addpackage")) to sHtml

            // The workspace moved to the PANEL HEADER (Nils 2026-08-15) - see Popup.
            Move (sHtml + (DivOpen("ap"))) to sHtml

            Move (sHtml + (HelpHeading("Local"))) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (HelpParagraph("A library on disk. Give an absolute or relative path to its " ;
                + (CodeText(".sws")) + ", or press " + (BoldText("Browse...")) + " to find it."))) to sHtml

            Move (sHtml + (HelpHeading("Cloud"))) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (HelpParagraph("A package from the DataFlex package catalogue, named " ;
                + (CodeText("<publisher>/<package>#<version>")) ;
                + ". The version is optional and may be a range. To see what is available, close this dialog and press " ;
                + (BoldText("Browse Packages...")) + "."))) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (BulletList((BulletItem("DataFlex-dev/Security#^1.0.0")) ;
                + (BulletItem("DataFlex-dev/WebChart#1.4.2")) ;
                + (BulletItem("DataFlex-dev/WebChart"))))) to sHtml

            Move (sHtml + '<h4>Git</h4>' + (HelpParagraph('Straight from a git server, as <code>&lt;gitUrl&gt;/&lt;pathToSws&gt;#&lt;tagOrBranch&gt;</code>. The path may be left out when a <code>df.sws</code> sits in the repository root, and the tag or branch is optional too. Needs a git client on the PATH. The path must name a <code>.sws</code> that really exists in the repository ' + CS_EmDash + ' a wrong name is refused with &quot;Failed to configure&quot;.'))) to sHtml
            /* THE TWO LIBRARIES NEARLY EVERY LEGACY WORKSPACE CARRIES (Nils 2026-08-17): vwin32fh and
               VDFQuery, as an "Examples:" line and two plain, selectable strings to copy into the
               field (Nils: not links). Both were verified against df-cli on the day they were written.
               The names sit here verbatim because a wrong-name refusal is a fact about upstream:
               vwin32fh's newest header in that repository is DF250 (the library compiles on 25 and
               26 - one code base with compile-time gates), and VDFQuery20 is the last release, kept
               as the migration aid it is (the NilsSve build since 2026-09-05 - see the Define). The
               tooltips say which library each is. */
            Move (sHtml + (ParaHtml("exl", "Examples:"))) to sHtml
            // THE LINKS SCROLL IN A BOX OF THEIR OWN (Nils 2026-10-17), from here to the end of the help:
            // both lists and the rule between them, under the "Examples:" line, which stays put. The box
            // takes the rest of the help box's height (addpackage.css .exscroll).
            Move (sHtml + (DivOpen("exscroll"))) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + '<ul class="ex">') to sHtml
            /* A Copy link per example (Nils 2026-08-21). A TEXT LINK since 2026-08-24, not a
               chip: a bordered button beside a line whose whole purpose is to be copied put two
               competing affordances on one row. It still comes out of ButtonHtml, which is what
               wires the click; only the styling moved (addpackage.css). The line stays selectable - some
               people will still drag across it - but a URL carrying a path INSIDE the repository is
               exactly the string a hand-selection clips short, and clipping it is what produces
               "Failed to configure". One click cannot mis-select.

               THE LABEL NEVER CHANGES (Nils 2026-08-21: "Don't change the text on the Copy Link
               button after a click"). It said "Copied" for the last-clicked chip; a button whose
               text moves under the pointer is worse than one that simply stays put, and the paste
               is its own confirmation. Nothing here reads any per-click state as a result. Since
               2026-10-17 the click also fills the Package field (DoCopyExample) - a confirmation the
               user sees at once. */
            Move (sHtml + '<li title="vwin32fh, Windows file handling - the DF26 header in the NilsSve fork, which is the copy DFRefactor itself consumes. Note the path INSIDE the repository: this library keeps its .sws files in StudioLibrary, and leaving that folder out is what makes an install fail with Failed to configure.">' + CS_ApExampleVwin32fh) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (ButtonHtml("span", "excp", "apcopy|1", "", "Copy link", "Put this whole line on the clipboard, including the path inside the repository.", True))) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + '</li>') to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + '<li title="VDFQuery20, the last VDFQuery release (a migration aid, no longer developed), in the NilsSve version for DataFlex 26: it ships no vwin32fh copy of its own and brings the vwin32fh package in as its dependency.">' + CS_ApExampleVdfQuery) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (ButtonHtml("span", "excp", "apcopy|2", "", "Copy link", "Put this whole line on the clipboard.", True))) to sHtml
            // Says in the open what the <li> title has only ever said on hover (Nils 2026-08-24).
            Move (sHtml + (((SpanOpen("exnote")) + 'The last version of VDFQuery, in the NilsSve version that depends on the vwin32fh package instead of bundling an old copy.') + CS_SpanEnd)) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + '</li>') to sHtml

            // Stables20, the successor of StureApsPublicLib (Nils 2026-10-13).
            Move (sHtml + '<li title="Stables20, previously called StureApsPublicLib. Use this package instead of the obsolete StureApsPublicLib library. Fully backward compatible.">' + CS_ApExampleStables) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (ButtonHtml("span", "excp", "apcopy|8", "", "Copy link", "Put this whole line on the clipboard.", True))) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (((SpanOpen("exnote")) + 'Stables20, previously called StureApsPublicLib. Use this package instead of the obsolete StureApsPublicLib library. Fully backward compatible.') + CS_SpanEnd)) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + '</li>') to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + '<li title="SigCj, the VDF SIG UK wrapper classes for the Codejock ActiveX controls, in the NilsSve fork for DataFlex 26 and Codejock 24.3.0. Upstream stops at DataFlex 25; this is the same library brought forward, and it covers DataFlex 27 too because 27 ships the same Codejock.">' + CS_ApExampleSigCj) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (ButtonHtml("span", "excp", "apcopy|6", "", "Copy link", "Put this whole line on the clipboard.", True))) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (((SpanOpen("exnote")) + 'Codejock wrapper classes for DataFlex 26 and later. The three controls DataFlex ships work as they are; the rest need Codejock SuitePro.') + CS_SpanEnd)) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + '</li>') to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + '</ul>') to sHtml

            /* THE SHELF, under its own rule (Nils 2026-08-30). The rows above are the libraries a
               legacy workspace almost certainly needs; these are ones it might WANT, and the
               separator says they are a different offer rather than four more of the same.

               Each says what the library does. The two rows above can get away with a name alone
               because anyone migrating already knows what they are for; nobody tries a library they
               cannot identify, so a description is the whole point of the row. */
            Move (sHtml + '<hr class="exrule">') to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (ParaHtml("exl", "More packages from RDC Tools, added the same way:"))) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + '<ul class="ex">') to sHtml

            Move (sHtml + '<li title="DbUpdateFramework - carries a database schema forward in versioned steps, applied when the program starts.">' + CS_ApExampleDuf) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (ButtonHtml("span", "excp", "apcopy|3", "", "Copy link", "Put this whole line on the clipboard.", True))) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (((SpanOpen("exnote")) + 'Versioned database schema updates, applied at startup. Brings RDCToolsLib, DFAbout and vWin32fh with it.') + CS_SpanEnd)) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + '</li>') to sHtml

            Move (sHtml + '<li title="The Data Folder Selector Utility helps users select which Data folder to use when starting a program.">' + CS_ApExampleDfs) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (ButtonHtml("span", "excp", "apcopy|4", "", "Copy link", "Put this whole line on the clipboard.", True))) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (((SpanOpen("exnote")) + 'Lets the user choose which Data folder a program starts against.') + CS_SpanEnd)) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + '</li>') to sHtml

            Move (sHtml + '<li title="Holiday and other special dates function library.">' + CS_ApExampleHolidays) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (ButtonHtml("span", "excp", "apcopy|5", "", "Copy link", "Put this whole line on the clipboard.", True))) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (((SpanOpen("exnote")) + 'Holidays and other special dates - working days, week numbers and the rest.') + CS_SpanEnd)) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + '</li>') to sHtml

            Move (sHtml + '<li title="RDCFlexTron - themed FlexTron hosts, web controls and modal panels, HTML markup builders and inline SVG icons for DataFlex Windows programs. It needs a Web UI theme package as well, for example DataFlex-dev/Web UI Material Theme.">' + CS_ApExampleFlexTron) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (ButtonHtml("span", "excp", "apcopy|7", "", "Copy link", "Put this whole line on the clipboard.", True))) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + (((SpanOpen("exnote")) + 'Themed FlexTron pages, web controls and modal panels. Brings RDCToolsLib and Web UI FlexTron with it; add a Web UI theme package too.') + CS_SpanEnd)) to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + '</li>') to sHtml

            Move (sHtml + '</ul>') to sHtml
            Move (sHtml + CS_DivEnd) to sHtml   // .exscroll
            Move (sHtml + CS_DivEnd) to sHtml   // .ap
            Function_Return sHtml
        End_Function

        Object oApHelp_hb is a cFTWebHtmlBox
            Set piColumnSpan  to 14
            // FILLS THE HOST under the Package row (Nils 2026-10-17: "perhaps all of the clickable links could
            // be in a scrollable area?"). The framework gives the box the height that is left, and
            // addpackage.css lays .ap out as a column in it: the three formats at the top, the example links
            // in their own scroll box (.exscroll) taking the rest - as the Libraries page scrolls its cards.
            Set pbFillHeight to True
            // DESIGN-TIME PLACEHOLDER for the Studio's Windows Designer, which models the LAST literal
            // psHtml it can parse. It is the string the runtime seeds (dumped by the cFTWebHtmlBox design
            // dump, no workspace loaded); the runtime expression sits in End_Construct_Object below.
            Set psHtml to """
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="RDCFlexTron/palette.css">
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="RDCFlexTron/buttons.css">
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="RDCFlexTron/bars.css">
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="CssStyle/addpackage.css">
            <div class="ap">
                <h4>Local</h4>
                <p>A library on disk. Give an absolute or relative path to its <code>.sws</code>, or press <b>Browse...</b> to find it.</p>
                <h4>Cloud</h4>
                <p>A package from the DataFlex package catalogue, named <code>&lt;publisher&gt;/&lt;package&gt;#&lt;version&gt;</code>. The version is optional and may be a range. To see what is
                    available, close this dialog and press <b>Browse Packages...</b>.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>DataFlex-dev/Security#^1.0.0</li>
                    <li>DataFlex-dev/WebChart#1.4.2</li>
                    <li>DataFlex-dev/WebChart</li></ul>
                <h4>Git</h4>
                <p>Straight from a git server, as <code>&lt;gitUrl&gt;/&lt;pathToSws&gt;#&lt;tagOrBranch&gt;</code>. The path may be left out when a <code>df.sws</code> sits in the repository root,
                    and the tag or branch is optional too. Needs a git client on the PATH. The path must name a <code>.sws</code> that really exists in the repository &mdash; a wrong name is refused with &quot;Failed to configure&quot;.</p>
                <p class="exl">Examples:</p>
                <div class="exscroll">
                    <ul class="ex">
                        <li
                            title="vwin32fh, Windows file handling - the DF26 header in the NilsSve fork, which is the copy DFRefactor itself consumes. Note the path INSIDE the repository: this
                            library keeps its .sws files in StudioLibrary, and leaving that folder out is what makes an install fail with Failed to
                            configure.">https:/&#47;github.com/NilsSve/Library-vwin32fh.git/StudioLibrary/vWin32fh-Library-DF26.0.sws<span class="excp" data-ServerOnClick="apcopy|1" title="Put this
                            whole line on the clipboard, including the path inside the repository.">Copy link</span></li>
                        <li
                            title="VDFQuery20, the last VDFQuery release (a migration aid, no longer developed), in the NilsSve version for DataFlex 26: it ships no vwin32fh copy of its own and brings
                            the vwin32fh package in as its dependency.">https:/&#47;github.com/NilsSve/VDFQuery20.git/VDFQuery20.sws<span class="excp" data-ServerOnClick="apcopy|2" title="Put this
                            whole line on the clipboard.">Copy link</span><span class="exnote">The last version of VDFQuery, in the NilsSve version that depends on the vwin32fh package instead of bundling an old copy.</span></li>
                        <li
                            title="Stables20, previously called StureApsPublicLib. Use this package instead of the obsolete StureApsPublicLib library. Fully backward
                            compatible.">https:/&#47;github.com/DataFlexCode/Stables20.git/Stables26.sws<span class="excp" data-ServerOnClick="apcopy|8" title="Put this whole line on the
                            clipboard.">Copy link</span><span class="exnote">Stables20, previously called StureApsPublicLib. Use this package instead of the obsolete StureApsPublicLib library. Fully backward compatible.</span></li>
                        <li
                            title="SigCj, the VDF SIG UK wrapper classes for the Codejock ActiveX controls, in the NilsSve fork for DataFlex 26 and Codejock 24.3.0. Upstream stops at DataFlex 25; this
                            is the same library brought forward, and it covers DataFlex 27 too because 27 ships the same
                            Codejock.">https:/&#47;github.com/NilsSve/Library-SigCj.git/SigCj-Library-DF26.0.sws<span class="excp" data-ServerOnClick="apcopy|6" title="Put this whole line on the
                            clipboard.">Copy link</span><span class="exnote">Codejock wrapper classes for DataFlex 26 and later. The three controls DataFlex ships work as they are; the rest need Codejock SuitePro.</span></li></ul>
                    <hr class="exrule">
                    <p class="exl">More packages from RDC Tools, added the same way:</p>
                    <ul class="ex">
                        <li
                            title="DbUpdateFramework - carries a database schema forward in versioned steps, applied when the program
                            starts.">https:/&#47;github.com/NilsSve/Library-DUF.git/RDC-DUF-Library.sws<span class="excp" data-ServerOnClick="apcopy|3" title="Put this whole line on the
                            clipboard.">Copy link</span><span class="exnote">Versioned database schema updates, applied at startup. Brings RDCToolsLib, DFAbout and vWin32fh with it.</span></li>
                        <li
                            title="The Data Folder Selector Utility helps users select which Data folder to use when starting a
                            program.">https:/&#47;github.com/NilsSve/Library-DataFolderSelector.git/RDC-DataFolderSelector-Library.sws<span class="excp" data-ServerOnClick="apcopy|4" title="Put this
                            whole line on the clipboard.">Copy link</span><span class="exnote">Lets the user choose which Data folder a program starts against.</span></li>
                        <li title="Holiday and other special dates function library.">https:/&#47;github.com/NilsSve/Library-HolidaysFuncLib.git/RDC-Holidays-Functions-Library.sws<span class="excp"
                            data-ServerOnClick="apcopy|5" title="Put this whole line on the clipboard.">Copy link</span><span class="exnote">Holidays and other special dates - working days, week numbers and the rest.</span></li>
                        <li
                            title="RDCFlexTron - themed FlexTron hosts, web controls and modal panels, HTML markup builders and inline SVG icons for DataFlex Windows programs. It needs a Web UI theme
                            package as well, for example DataFlex-dev/Web UI Material
                            Theme.">https:/&#47;github.com/NilsSve/Library-RDCFlexTron.git/RDC-FlexTron-Library.sws<span class="excp" data-ServerOnClick="apcopy|7" title="Put this whole line on the
                            clipboard.">Copy link</span><span class="exnote">Themed FlexTron pages, web controls and modal panels. Brings RDCToolsLib and Web UI FlexTron with it; add a Web UI theme package too.</span></li></ul></div></div>
            """

            // RUNTIME content - here rather than in the object body, so the Designer keeps the literal above.
            Procedure End_Construct_Object
                Forward Send End_Construct_Object
                Set psHtml to (HelpHtml(Self))
            End_Procedure

            /* After the web click has returned (the library's click relay), like the Browse chip: a Win32
               clipboard open/close stays off the WebView2 pump.

               THE PAYLOAD ARRIVES IN sId, NOT IN sParam. The framework does not split an id on "|";
               MaintainLibrariesFT has always known this ("If (Left(sId, 9) = \"mlpkgdel|\")") and I
               assumed the opposite here, so the first version tested "sId = \"apcopy\"" against an
               sId of "apcopy|1", never matched, and the chip did nothing at all (Nils 2026-08-21:
               "Trying the Copy link button for vWin32fh did not work"). "apcopy|" is 7 characters,
               so the tail starts at position 8. */
            Procedure OnHtmlClick String sId String sParam
                If (Left(sId, 7) = "apcopy|") ;
                    Send DoCopyExample of (oAddPackage_dg(Self)) (Mid(sId, (Length(sId) - 7), 8))
            End_Procedure
        End_Object

    End_Object

    /* THE BAND. Its own host, pinned to the dialog's bottom edge - see the panel comment for why
       the buttons may never live in the content host's flow again. */
    Object oApButtonsHost is a cFTGridHost
        /* The band's top TOUCHES the content host's bottom (2026-08-15, the colour probe): the
           white resize stripe above the buttons was the bare panel strip BETWEEN the hosts -
           its erase brush flashes white before the dark paint lands, and neither host's
           background covers it. No gap, no strip, nothing to flash. The clearance below the
           band (to the status bar) keeps the earlier measure. */
        Set Location to 355 4
        Set Size to 20 552
        Set peAnchors to anBottomLeftRight
        /* OK, Cancel, Help: framework buttons (cFTWebButton, RDCFlexTron) on 8 px columns, where a button's
           span is its width - so they keep their place and gap at any size, the drift that once kept them in
           one HTML control (Nils 2026-08-14). Column 0 takes the rest of the width, so they sit bottom-right.
           Each button's work runs in its OnButtonClick, after the web click has returned: OK and Cancel close
           the panel there, and Help's browser launch needs no timer. OK first, then Cancel - the order every
           other dialog here uses - and Help last. Spans fit the captions, at the 78 px least. */
        Set piColumnCount to 35         // column 0, then OK's 11, Cancel's 12 and Help's 11
        Set psColumnWidths to "0/1fr"   // column 0 takes the extra width

        /* OK IS ALWAYS LIVE (2026-08-15 evening - "pressing OK, absolutely nothing happens"). It used to
           light only after the field's OnChange had run, and a web form fires OnChange on BLUR - so
           paste-then-click-OK never blurred the field and the click went nowhere, silently. A button that
           lies about a filled field is worse than one that says "name a package first"; DoOk answers the
           blank case in words. */
        Object oApOkBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piColumnIndex to 1
            Set piColumnSpan to 11
            Set psCaption to "OK"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftg-check"

            Procedure OnButtonClick
                Send DoOk of (oAddPackage_dg(Self))
            End_Procedure
        End_Object

        Object oApCancelBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piColumnIndex to 12
            Set piColumnSpan to 12
            Set psCaption to "Cancel"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftg-close"

            Procedure OnButtonClick
                Send DoCancel of (oAddPackage_dg(Self))
            End_Procedure
        End_Object

        /* HELP LAST IN THE BAND, and it is the one button here that changes nothing. The notes under the
           field already name the three forms; this opens the illustrated walkthrough for the git one, which
           is the form nobody gets right first time - the string is two things joined, and the join is a
           slash the user types. */
        Object oApHelpBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piColumnIndex to 24
            Set piColumnSpan to 11
            Set psCaption to "Help"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftg-help"
            Set psToolTip to "Open the illustrated walkthrough: how to build the git string from a repository page. Opens in your browser."

            Procedure OnButtonClick
                Send DoShowGuide of (oAddPackage_dg(Self))
            End_Procedure
        End_Object
    End_Object

    /* Open the illustrated walkthrough in the default browser.

       IN THE BROWSER, NOT IN A PANEL. The page is a read-alongside reference - you follow it with
       the repository open in one window and this dialog in another - so a modal that has to be
       dismissed to use the thing it explains would be the wrong container. It also keeps the guide
       ordinary HTML that can be opened, printed or bookmarked on its own.

       Found through pOrgWS, which is DFRefactor's OWN workspace - psAppHtmlPath of phoWorkspace is
       the TARGET workspace's AppHtml, and pointing at that would look for our guide inside the
       customer's source tree. The packager copies AppHtml whole, so the file ships without a
       per-file list entry.

       A missing file is SAID, not swallowed: this is a deployment fault the user cannot deduce from
       a browser that never opened. */
    Procedure DoShowGuide
        tWorkspacePaths WS
        String sPath

        Get pOrgWS of ghoApplication to WS
        Move (vFolderFormat(WS.sAppHtml) + CS_ApGuideFile) to sPath
        If (vFilePathExists(sPath) = 0) Begin
            Send FTStopBox ("The walkthrough was not found at:" + Character(10) + Character(10) + "   " + sPath ;
                + Character(10) + Character(10) + "It ships in DFRefactor's own AppHtml folder - the installation looks incomplete.") "Guide not found"
            Procedure_Return
        End
        Send vShellExecute "open" sPath "" ""
    End_Procedure

    /* Puts a value into the Package field the user is looking at, and into psPackage - for Copy link and Browse...
       Both run after the click has returned, outside a web event, so (RDCFlexTron's FTPageIsUp.pkg): stored with
       Set, for a page that loads; pushed with WebSet to the page that is up; and sent NOW with CheckUpdateWebUI - a
       push made outside a web event otherwise waits for the host's next idle tick, and the field showed the value
       only once it was clicked into (Nils 2026-10-17). A plain Set alone reached no page at all. */
    Procedure FillPackageField String sValue
        Handle hoHost hoForm
        Move (oWebHost(Self)) to hoHost
        Move (oApPkg_wf(hoHost)) to hoForm
        Set psValue of hoForm to sValue
        If (FTHostPageIsUp(hoHost)) Begin
            WebSet psValue of hoForm to sValue
            Send CheckUpdateWebUI of hoHost
        End
        Set psPackage to sValue
        Send RefreshOkState
    End_Procedure

    /* Put one example URL into the Package field, ready for OK - the way Browse... fills it with a
       picked .sws (Nils 2026-10-17: "to also paste the content to the Package: form") - and on the
       clipboard, through rfSetClipboardText (RefactorFileIO.pkg), the one way onto it, which says when
       the clipboard could not be opened: a copy that silently did not happen is worse than none, so
       that gets its own words here. The field comes first, so a failed copy still leaves it filled. */
    Procedure DoCopyExample String sWhich
        String sUrl
        Boolean bOk

        If (sWhich = "8") ;
            Move CS_ApExampleStables to sUrl
        Else If (sWhich = "7") ;
            Move CS_ApExampleFlexTron to sUrl
        Else If (sWhich = "6") ;
            Move CS_ApExampleSigCj to sUrl
        Else If (sWhich = "5") ;
            Move CS_ApExampleHolidays to sUrl
        Else If (sWhich = "4") ;
            Move CS_ApExampleDfs to sUrl
        Else If (sWhich = "3") ;
            Move CS_ApExampleDuf to sUrl
        Else If (sWhich = "2") ;
            Move CS_ApExampleVdfQuery to sUrl
        Else ;
            Move CS_ApExampleVwin32fh to sUrl

        Send FillPackageField sUrl

        Get rfSetClipboardText sUrl to bOk
        If (bOk = False) Begin
            Send FTStopBox "The clipboard could not be opened, so nothing was copied. The Package field has the address." "Copy link"
            Procedure_Return
        End
        // Nothing is re-rendered: the chip's label never changes, so the dialog is already correct.
    End_Procedure

    Procedure DoBrowseLocal
        Boolean bOpen
        String[] asFileNames
        String sFileName
        Get Show_Dialog of (oOpenSwsDialog(Self)) to bOpen
        If (bOpen = False) ;
            Procedure_Return
        Get Selected_Files of (oOpenSwsDialog(Self)) to asFileNames
        Move asFileNames[0] to sFileName
        If (Trim(sFileName) <> "") Begin
            Send FillPackageField sFileName
        End
    End_Procedure

    /* THE BAND IS NEVER RE-RENDERED FROM HERE (Nils 2026-08-17: "I have to click OK twice for
       anything to happen"). The old body re-drew the button band whenever blank/non-blank flipped -
       and the flip arrives at the WORST moment: pressing the mouse on OK (the band's host) takes
       focus from the field (the other host), the field's OnChange reaches the server first, this
       flipped pbOkLit and UpdateHtml'd the band, and the DOM under the pointer was replaced between
       mousedown and mouseup - so the browser never fired the click. The second click landed. It was
       also work for nothing: ButtonsHtml has drawn OK always-live since 08-15 and ignores the flag,
       so the re-render swapped identical markup. pbOkLit is still tracked (cheap, and DoOk's blank
       refusal is the real guard); the band's buttons never change. */
    Procedure RefreshOkState
        String sPkg
        Get psPackage to sPkg
        Set pbOkLit to (Trim(sPkg) <> "")
    End_Procedure

    // Nothing is validated here beyond "not blank". df-cli is the authority on what its own grammar
    // accepts, and it says so clearly when it does not - guessing at the rules in advance would only
    // add a second, wronger opinion.
    /* THE CLICK COMMITS THE FIELD FIRST. psPackage is filled by the field's OnChange, which fires
       on blur - and a click on OK in the OTHER host does not blur the field first, so
       the freshest paste may not be in psPackage yet. WebGet psValue is the codebase's own idiom
       for reading a live web-form value from a server handler (CompilerSetupFT does exactly this
       from its Select click). Empty after that is genuinely empty, and is said. */
    Procedure DoOk
        String sPkg sLive
        WebGet psValue of (oApPkg_wf(oWebHost(Self))) to sLive
        If (Trim(sLive) <> "") ;
            Set psPackage to sLive
        Get psPackage to sPkg
        If (Trim(sPkg) = "") Begin
            Send FTInfoBox "Name a package first - a publisher/package#version, a git url, or a path to a local .sws. The three forms are described below the field." "Nothing to add"
            Procedure_Return
        End
        Set pbConfirmed to True
        Send Close_Panel
    End_Procedure

    Procedure DoCancel
        Set pbConfirmed to False
        Set psPackage to ""
        Send Close_Panel
    End_Procedure

    // Fresh every time: a package string left over from a previous popup would read as consent the
    // user never gave this time.
    Procedure Popup
        // The header names the workspace (Nils 2026-08-15: "append it to the Add package text") -
        // it was a body line, where it pushed the real help down.
        Set Label to ("Add package - " + psSwsFile(Self))
        Set psPackage   to ""
        Set pbConfirmed to False
        Set psValue of (oApPkg_wf(oWebHost(Self))) to ""
        Send RefreshOkState
        Send UpdateHtml of (oApHelp_hb(oWebHost(Self))) (HelpHtml(oWebHost(Self)))
        Forward Send Popup
    End_Procedure
End_Object

/*  Ask for a package to add to sSwsFile. Returns the string the user entered, or "" if they
    cancelled - it is passed to df-cli exactly as typed.

        Get PromptForPackage sSws to sPackage

    Global, so the Libraries dialog and anything later can reach it.  */
Function PromptForPackage Global String sSwsFile Returns String
    Handle ho
    Boolean bOk
    String sPkg

    Move (oAddPackage_dg(Self)) to ho
    Set psSwsFile of ho to sSwsFile
    Send Popup of ho
    Get pbConfirmed of ho to bOk
    If (bOk = False) ;
        Function_Return ""
    Get psPackage of ho to sPkg
    Function_Return (Trim(sPkg))
End_Function
